To find the area of the region in the \(xOy\) coordinate system consisting of all points \((x, y)\) that satisfy \(\lfloor x \rfloor \cdot \lfloor y \rfloor = 2013\), we start by recalling that the floor function \(\lfloor x \rfloor\) gives the greatest integer less than or equal to \(x\). Let \(m = \lfloor x \rfloor\) and \(n = \lfloor y \rfloor\). The condition becomes \(m \cdot n = 2013\). 

